.env
.env.local
# Deployment secrets: database passwords, SMTP credentials and the field
# encryption key. `.env.production.example` beside it is the template, and is
# the only one of the two that belongs in the repository.
.env.production
# Same, for the staging project. It holds a *separate* set of secrets — nothing
# is copied from .env.production, and rotating one environment must never touch
# another. `.env.staging.example` beside it is the template.
.env.staging
*.log
